SUMMARY:Dec 18th Community Cuddles
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Cuddle Collective\nPlease note- If you want to atten
 d this event you need to purchase a ticket- We advertise in many places an
 d only paid tickets will reserve your space. use the link below to reserve
  your **[https://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/friday-dec-18th-community-c
 uddle](https://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/friday-dec-18th-community-cud
 dle)**\n\n**This is a non-sexual touch based event that invites participan
 ts to explore platonic intimacy in a safe environment** with like-minded p
 eople. We respect personal boundaries and through a supportive framework o
 f mutual agreements that maximize safety and create a space of easy openne
 ss and compassionate connection.\nAt this event we have the chance to norm
 alize touch with clear boundaries\; this is a space for respectful\, conse
 nt-based touch. We allow ourselves to be seen. We have fun.\nWe welcome pe
 ople of all backgrounds\, genders\, ethnicities\, relationship styles\, se
 xualities\, sizes\, and ages (18+).\n\n**THE RULES**\n\n1. Clothes stay on
  for the whole event.\n2. You do not have to touch anyone at this event.\n
 3. You must receive a verbal YES before you touch anyone.\n4. Take care of
  yourself and those you choose to interact with.\n5. Speak up if you have 
 a question\, concern\, or if you need assistance with anything during the 
 event.\n6. All emotions are welcome- we love vulnerability.\n**WHY CUDDLE?
 **\nTouch is a basic human need\, and many of us do not get enough\; most 
 people don’t even know they are missing touch\, or have a way to ask for
  touch without sexualizing it. We believe deeply in the power of touch\, a
 nd the importance of communication and consent in creating a safe space fo
 r touch.\nCUDDLING WITH STRANGERS\nCuddling with strangers sounds weird or
  scary to most people. “Will I like it?” “What if someone wants to t
 ouch me and I don’t want to?” “What if I say yes and it’s not what
  I want?” “What if I really want to touch someone and they say no?” 
 These are all normal questions. The answer is that this is a space created
  to ask for exactly what you want\, and receive NOTHING you don’t want. 
 Many people start out nervous at a cuddle event & most are really glad the
 y came.\n\n**Schedule:**\n6:50-7pm: Arrive with snacks to share! Get comfo
 rtable\, meet\, mingle\, & snack.\n7:05pm: Welcome Circle- its mandatory. 
 We will set our container\, talk about personal boundaries\, communication
 \, & consent.\n7:15pm: Icebreakers and connective activities.\n8:00pm: Ope
 n cuddling! You MUST ask and get a verbal ‘yes’ before touching or cud
 dling with anybody at this event. If you are not sure how to do this – g
 reat! – we will talk about it during the welcome circle.\n10:50pm: Closi
 ng Circle\, cleanup and head home.\n**ETIQUETTE**\n\n\\*ARRIVE ON TIME: It
  is important that all participants arrive before the Welcome Circle. The 
 Welcome Circle serves the purpose of creating the safe space for consensua
 l\, non-sexual touch between participants and making sure that everyone is
  informed about consent.\n\n* Please arrive clean & as scent free as possi
 ble.\n\\*BE SOBER: Please do not drink or smoke before or at this event.\n
 \n**WHAT TO BRING:** personal water bottle and snacks to share\, a friend\
 , a date – whatever cuddle accessories you like! The only thing that you
  are required to bring is a clean and sober you.\n\nThese events are not "
 gender balanced".\n\n**We take individual and group safety seriously!** If
  you experience\, see\, or know that one of our participants is not safe t
 o be at this event we want to know about it. We are committed to doing our
  best to create a safe environment which means that if someone is causing 
 harm (physical or mental) that person is not welcome here (this includes h
 arm that takes place outside of our events). We stand behind survivors and
  know that some of our participants are here to heal from touch based trau
 ma.\n\n\\*refund policy-\nFull refund if you cancel 7 days before the even
 t or you cancel due to illness\, emergency\, or direct exposure to covid/f
 lu.\nCredit towards a future event if you cancel more than 3 days before a
 n event.\nNo refund if you cancel within 2 days of the event or no-show.
