SUMMARY:Dec 19th An Evening of Spicy/Sensual Snuggles
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Cuddle Collective\nPlease note- If you want to atten
 d this event you need to purchase a ticket- We advertise in many places an
 d only paid tickets will reserve your space. use the link below to reserve
  your ticket-\nhttps://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/sat-dec-19th-an-eveni
 ng-of-sensual-snuggles\n\nWhat is a Sensual Snuggle Event?\\*\\*\nThis is 
 a sweet & welcoming event where we practice and use verbal consent to conn
 ect and share touch. We talk about boundaries and practice both saying and
  receiving a “no”. In this space it is common to see people cuddle\, s
 hare massage\, have their hair brushed\, kiss\, expose nipples\, play\, la
 ugh\, cry\, and be vulnerable. This is a sober space where we can relax an
 d connect with other humans who are seeking touch based connection.\nWe st
 rive for this to be a safe event. Safe touch enhances our ability to conne
 ct with and trust people. When we are in a space of safety\, we are able t
 o relax\, feel comfort\, and be vulnerable.\n\n**Our Agreements:**\n1- We 
 ask for what we want an wait for a yes before touching others.\n2- We say 
 no if we don’t want to do something.\n3- We try to receive a no with gra
 ce and not take it personally.\n4- We arrive on time\, clean (as scent fre
 e as possible)\, and sober.\n5- We keep our pants/shorts on at this event.
  (Tops are optional\; this is a sensual space\, not a sexual space.)\n6- W
 e are here to connect with others. Connection can be verbal\, platonic\, o
 r spicy!\n7- We welcome diversity. Isms and Phobias are not welcome here!\
 n\n**Who should attend:**\nPeople who are interested in safely exploring t
 ouch and sensuality with strangers. This includes people who are single\, 
 people who are not single\, couples\, folks who are new to town and lookin
 g for connection\, people of all/any genders and sexual orientations\, peo
 ple of all ages (18 and up). People who understand and respect consent\, w
 ho will take care of themselves and people around them. This event is quee
 r-normative. The guest list will include all genders\, orientations\, ages
 \, and personalities. If that’s not your thing… This is not the event 
 for you.\n***Who should NOT attend:***\n-People who are only looking for a
  sex party.\n-People who do not understand and respect consent.\n-People w
 ho have extreme fear of setting and speaking their personal boundaries\; i
 n order to create a safe space we need to know that you will say “no” 
 if you feel a no.\n-People who are homophobic\, racist\, sexist\, ageist\,
  ableist…\n-People under 18 years of age.\n***Schedule of the Evening***
 \n\n\\*6:50pm Doors Open\, Mix & Mingle\n\n* 7:00pm We gather in a circle 
 to meet each other\, build a container\, cover consent and boundary settin
 g and discuss event agreements. Then we will play a few intimacy building 
 games to meet and connect with other people in the room. Please make sure 
 you arrive on-time!\n\\*8:15pm Once the container is built we will have se
 lf directed snuggling and sensual interactions until the end of the party.
 \n* 10:50pm Closing Circle\; a time to re-center and connect as a group to
  verbally share anything that came up at the event or to voice gratitude t
 o someone(s) you enjoyed interacting with.\n\\*11:00pm cleanup & head home
 \; you are welcome to help.\n\n**We take individual and group safety serio
 usly!** If you experience\, see\, or know that one of our participants is 
 not safe to be at this event we want to know about it. We are committed to
  doing our best to create a safe environment which means that if someone i
 s causing harm (physical or mental) that person is not welcome here (this 
 includes harm that takes place outside of our events). We stand behind sur
 vivors and know that some of our participants are here to heal from touch 
 based trauma.\n\nThese events are not "gender balanced"[. Check out our we
 bsite for more information about this decision.](http://holdmeavl.com/why-
 i-dont-gender-balance-events/)\n\n**Simple definitions/clarifications-** P
 latonic- marked by the absence of romance or sex.\nMost of the interaction
 s we have with friends and strangers are platonic.\nSensual- gratification
  of the senses or the indulgence of appetite.\nWe might feel sensual when 
 we feel someone's breath on our neck or experience a extra long and slow c
 aress.\nSexual- having or involving sex.\nOften involving one more more pe
 oples genitals\; perhaps seeking orgasm.\n\\*Refund Policy- Full refund if
  you cancel 7 days before the event or you cancel due to illness\, emergen
 cy\, or direct exposure to covid. Credit towards a future event if you can
 cel more than 3 days before an event. No refund if you cancel within 2 day
 s of the event or no-show.
